Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue, but it is two.** The desk merged every report with a matching subject line
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by cause, the reports split in two:

- `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day first. This is
  the bug the queued fix is for. Tracked in [{tickets.parser.label}]({tickets.parser.href}).
- `hint`: booking-v3's date field shows `MM/DD/YYYY` but reads the date day first. Only through the
  form of the three tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it. Tracked in
  [{tickets.hint.label}]({tickets.hint.href}).

The full split, with how each report was placed: [#4471 split](/kb/incidents/4471-split).

<Callout kind="warn">
Split. Two problems, two tickets. The queued parser fix closes only the first.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A big ticket can hold more than one bug. Same subject line is not the same cause: check the
  tenant's booking form and the report body before merging.
- Count each report once. The export repeats rows when its pages overlap.
- Keep the page in step with the data. This page said "one issue, one fix queued" while its own
  table showed a second cause with no ticket.
